      bio: '<ul><li>Drafted by Ottawa in the 9th round (53rd overall) in the 2023 PWHL Draft.</li><li>Signed a one-year contract with Boston on June 20, 2025, through the 2025-26 season.</li><li>During her second year in Ottawa, Boyd appeared in 23 regular season games and all eight playoff matchups throughout the Charge&rsquo;s run to the PWHL Finals.</li><li>Played a season-high 25:48 TOI on May 24 against the Minnesota Frost in Game 3 of the Walter Cup Finals.</li><li>During the inaugural season, Boyd recorded three points in the first four games (Jan. 2-23, 2024).</li><li>While at Quinnipiac University, she played in the Frozen Fenway 2023 Game, inside MLB&rsquo;s oldest active ballpark, where the Bobcats cruised to a 3-1 victory against the Harvard Crimson. In that game, she faced childhood friend (and former PWHL Ottawa teammate) Kristin Della Rovere.</li><li>Served as co-captain at Quinnipiac for her final season (2022-23), along with Seattle Torrent&rsquo;s Lexie Adzija.</li><li>Served as assistant captain during her junior (2021-22) season where she played 35 games, recorded 13 points, blocked 46 shots and was named to the ECAC Third Team All-League.</li><li>Earned the Bobcats Coaches Award during her senior season for instilling strong leadership foundations.</li><li>Represented Canada at the 2018 IIHF U-18 Women&rsquo;s World Championships. Won a bronze medal while serving as alternate captain.</li><li>Launched a podcast called &ldquo;No Straight Answers&rdquo; on June 29, 2025.</li></ul>',
